@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Experimental RAM desktop project
+
+This producer prepares a small desktop from normal Omarchy build inputs.
+It is separate from the installed root and installer recovery. No device has
+qualified this project yet; the first stage provides host selection, limits,
+receipts and runtime source for review.
+
+## Inputs
+
+Use the kept root directory produced by the normal `system/assemble-rootfs`,
+its `rootfs.tar.gz.json` and `packages.lock`, and the matching verified normal
+`desktop/build` component. Run in that Arch native build environment so file
+ownership can be preserved. Nothing is extracted from the historical lab root.
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/build-ram-desktop.py \
+  --root STAGED_ROOT --desktop DESKTOP_COMPONENT \
+  --source-receipt ROOTFS_RECEIPT --packages-lock PACKAGES_LOCK \
+  --orchard ORCHARD_CHECKOUT --output NEW_PLAN --plan-only
+```
+
+After reviewing the plan, use a different new output directory and omit
+`--plan-only` to build. The host needs `readelf` and `mksquashfs`. The producer
+calls the normal desktop verifier, checks that the staged root carries its UI
+manifest and matches the package lock, and records each selected byte hash.
+It records the normal base archive receipt; it does not re-read that archive
+or claim that every unselected file of the staged directory was checked.
+
+The source root must be the normal base stage. The finished release root
+rewrites the UI manifest; accepting that later stage needs a separate matching
+receipt contract, rather than ignoring a manifest mismatch.
+
+## Selection and limits
+
+The initial profile keeps Labwc, Quickshell, the normal keyboard and UI,
+Foot, session tools and their ELF interpreters/dependencies. Runtime seeds
+include QML, Wayland Qt plugins, fonts, xkb, locale, NSS/account information,
+CA certificates and D-Bus/input data. Script interpreters and the Python
+standard library are included when needed. Optional GTK platform themes and
+non-SQLite Qt SQL backends are outside this session.
+
+This is an explicit first profile, not proof of every runtime `dlopen`, QML
+import, helper or optional panel dependency. Missing files/dependencies and
+limits refuse a build. Large applications such as browsers are not included.
+
+- Selected regular files: at most 384 MiB and 25,000 files.
+- Gzip SquashFS image: at most 128 MiB, 256 KiB blocks, one build worker.
+- Writable overlay: default 64 MiB, configurable only between 16 and 128 MiB.
+- Desktop `/run`: a separate 32 MiB tmpfs.
+- Desktop `/dev/shm`: a separate 16 MiB tmpfs.
+
+These are bounds, not a measurement of free RAM or peak desktop use. The
+kernel, framebuffers, runtime allocations and page cache also need room. Zram
+is not enabled by this first profile and is not additional physical RAM.
+
+## Ordinary Orchard build and run
+
+The output's `project/` is a normal `orchard.toml` RAM project:
+
+```sh
+ORCHARD_CHECKOUT/bin/orchard build OUTPUT/project --device BOARD --kernel-tree KERNEL_TREE
+ORCHARD_CHECKOUT/bin/orchard run OUTPUT/project --device BOARD --no-build
+```
+
+Use one coherent, qualified native kernel/DT/provider/module set. Orchard
+adds its ordinary USB session, matching modules and board firmware. The public
+J72 recipe still has no touch output until native qualification; private test
+firmware can be an explicit private `rootfs/lib/firmware` overlay before build.
+
+Boot starts only the tested style of rescue console, serial and key-authenticated
+SSH. PID 1 stays in the rescue initramfs, and automatic module/hotplug loading
+is disabled. No internal filesystem, charging policy, bus coldplug or optional
+touch module is started by init. After hardware checks and explicit normal
+module loading, the host can request the desktop through the usual transport:
+
+```sh
+ORCHARD_CHECKOUT/bin/orchard exec -- /usr/libexec/omarchy/ram-desktop start
+```
+
+The session mounts its SquashFS file read-only and adds the bounded tmpfs
+upper. It runs normal source-built Omarchy components in a chroot. USB shell
+and key paths remain outside that root; its private `/run` avoids recursive
+bind mounts and duplicate SSH ownership. Only existing input/DRM nodes are
+announced to its udev daemon. Process startup is reported separately from UI
+readiness. `ram-desktop stop` terminates only recorded process groups and
+unmounts normally; stuck cleanup retains ownership and reports failure.
+
+The RAM session uses the normal first-theme renderer, keyboard, Labwc
+configuration and panel. It has a private D-Bus session and seatd; it does not
+claim the installed systemd/PAM/greetd login or all optional desktop services.
+The profile explicitly sets `C.UTF-8` and includes its locale data.
+
+## Gates before device use
+
+Run the first real-root plan and inspect expanded size and closure; verify
+the image compressor, generated root and normal component provenance. Check
+normal startup/stop under a suitable Linux test environment, including failure
+cleanup and file ownership. Then measure native device RAM, UI/input/keyboard,
+USB-shell survival, unplugged operation and normal return to iOS. Host unit
+fixtures and shell syntax do not establish those results.
diff --git a/release/ram_desktop.py b/release/ram_desktop.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..33ffe9d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/ram_desktop.py
@@ -0,0 +1,305 @@
+"""A bounded RAM desktop from a normal staged Omarchy root; no device access."""
+from collections import deque
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath
+import re
+import shlex
+import shutil
+import stat
+import subprocess
+
+PROJECT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
+UI = 'home/tablet/.local/share/omarchy-ipad'
+PROGRAMS = ('labwc', 'qs', 'foot', 'bash', 'env', 'dbus-daemon', 'dbus-run-session', 'dbus-uuidgen',
+            'seatd', 'setpriv', 'wlr-randr', 'fc-cache', 'fc-match', 'udevadm',
+            'systemctl', 'cat', 'date', 'grep', 'sed', 'head', 'tail', 'tr', 'cut',
+            'mkdir', 'chmod', 'chown', 'cp', 'mv', 'rm', 'ln', 'readlink', 'id',
+            'sleep', 'kill', 'pkill', 'jq', 'socat', 'sort', 'stat', 'find', 'curl',
+            'awk', 'basename', 'dirname', 'mktemp', 'rmdir', 'gsettings')
+TREES = (UI, 'usr/local/bin', 'home/tablet/.config/labwc', 'home/tablet/.config/foot',
+         'home/tablet/.config/fontconfig', 'home/tablet/.config/omarchy-ipad',
+         'usr/lib/qt6/qml', 'usr/lib/qt6/plugins',
+         'usr/lib/udev/rules.d', 'usr/share/X11/xkb', 'etc/fonts',
+         'usr/share/fontconfig', 'usr/share/libinput', 'usr/share/dbus-1',
+         'etc/dbus-1', 'usr/lib/locale/C.utf8', 'etc/ssl/certs', 'usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas')
+FILES = ('etc/passwd', 'etc/group', 'etc/nsswitch.conf', 'etc/hosts',
+         'home/tablet/.bashrc', 'usr/lib/systemd/systemd-udevd', 'usr/lib/udev/libinput-device-group',
+         'usr/libexec/omarchy-wtype',
+         'usr/local/libexec/arch-ipad-scale-output', 'usr/local/libexec/arch-ipad-first-theme',
+         'usr/local/libexec/arch-ipad-rotate-output', 'usr/local/share/applications/foot.desktop',
+         'usr/share/terminfo/f/foot', 'usr/share/terminfo/x/xterm-256color',
+         'usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSans.ttf',
+         'usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSansMono.ttf',
+         'usr/share/fonts/TTF/JetBrainsMonoNerdFont-Regular.ttf')
+
+
+def digest(path):
+    h = hashlib.sha256()
+    with Path(path).open('rb') as stream:
+        for block in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b''):
+            h.update(block)
+    return h.hexdigest()
+
+
+def normalized(name):
+    result = []
+    for part in str(name).split('/'):
+        if part in ('', '.'):
+            continue
+        if part == '..':
+            if not result:
+                raise ValueError('Path escapes the source root')
+            result.pop()
+        else:
+            result.append(part)
+    return '/'.join(result)
+
+
+class Source:
+    def __init__(self, root):
+        self.root = Path(root).absolute()
+        if self.root.is_symlink() or not self.root.is_dir():
+            raise ValueError('Expected a real staged root directory')
+        self.links = {}
+
+    def resolve(self, name):
+        name = normalized(name)
+        for _ in range(32):
+            parts = name.split('/')
+            for index in range(len(parts)):
+                label = '/'.join(parts[:index + 1])
+                path = self.root / label
+                if path.is_symlink():
+                    target = os.readlink(path)
+                    self.links[label] = target
+                    base = '' if target.startswith('/') else '/'.join(parts[:index])
+                    name = normalized('/'.join((base, target, *parts[index + 1:])))
+                    break
+            else:
+                return name
+        raise ValueError('Source symlink cycle or excessive depth')
+
+
+def elf_dependencies(path):
+    with Path(path).open('rb') as stream:
+        header = stream.read(20)
+    if header[:4] != b'\x7fELF':
+        return [], [], None
+    if len(header) < 20 or header[4:6] != b'\x02\x01' or int.from_bytes(header[18:20], 'little') != 183:
+        raise ValueError('RAM desktop requires little-endian AArch64 ELF')
+    output = subprocess.check_output(['readelf', '-d', '-l', str(path)], text=True)
+    needed = re.findall(r'Shared library: \[([^\]]+)\]', output)
+    if any('/' in name or name in ('.', '..') for name in needed):
+        raise ValueError('Unsafe ELF library name')
+    paths = [p for group in re.findall(r'\((?:RUNPATH|RPATH)\).*?\[([^\]]+)\]', output)
+             for p in group.split(':') if p]
+    interpreters = re.findall(r'Requesting program interpreter: ([^\]]+)', output)
+    if len(interpreters) > 1:
+        raise ValueError('Multiple ELF interpreters')
+    return needed, paths, interpreters[0] if interpreters else None
+
+
+def selection(source, seeds, trees, *, expanded_limit=384 * 1024**2,
+              dependencies=elf_dependencies):
+    selected, pending, total = {}, deque(), 0
+
+    def add(name):
+        nonlocal total
+        label = source.resolve(name)
+        if label in selected:
+            return
+        path = source.root / label
+        if not path.is_file() or path.is_symlink():
+            raise ValueError('Missing selected regular file: ' + label)
+        info = path.stat()
+        if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode) or info.st_size > 128 * 1024**2:
+            raise ValueError('Special or oversized selected file: ' + label)
+        total += info.st_size
+        if total > expanded_limit or len(selected) >= 25000:
+            raise ValueError('RAM desktop subset exceeds its declared limit')
+        selected[label] = {'bytes': info.st_size, 'sha256': digest(path),
+                           'mode': stat.S_IMODE(info.st_mode), 'uid': info.st_uid, 'gid': info.st_gid}
+        pending.append(label)
+
+    for seed in seeds:
+        add(seed)
+    visited_trees = set()
+
+    def tree_files(tree):
+        resolved = source.resolve(tree)
+        parent = source.root / resolved
+        if not parent.is_dir():
+            raise ValueError('Missing runtime data directory: ' + tree)
+        if resolved in visited_trees:
+            return
+        visited_trees.add(resolved)
+        for path in sorted(parent.iterdir()):
+            if path.name in ('__pycache__', 'test', 'tests', 'idlelib', 'tkinter', 'site-packages'):
+                continue
+            label = path.relative_to(source.root).as_posix()
+            # This session uses the native Wayland QPA and SQLite only. GTK
+            # platform themes and optional SQL backends require other desktops.
+            if '/plugins/platformthemes/' in label or ('/plugins/sqldrivers/' in label and
+                                                        path.name != 'libqsqlite.so'):
+                continue
+            actual = source.root / source.resolve(label)
+            if actual.is_dir():
+                tree_files(label)
+            elif actual.is_file():
+                add(label)
+            else:
+                raise ValueError('Special runtime data member')
+
+    for tree in trees:
+        tree_files(tree)
+    python_added = False
+    while pending:
+        label = pending.popleft()
+        with (source.root / label).open('rb') as stream:
+            head = stream.readline(4096)
+        if head.startswith(b'#!'):
+            fields = shlex.split(head[2:].decode().strip())
+            if not fields or not fields[0].startswith('/'):
+                raise ValueError('Invalid script interpreter: ' + label)
+            add(fields[0])
+            if fields[0] == '/usr/bin/env':
+                if len(fields) < 2 or fields[1].startswith('-') or '/' in fields[1]:
+                    raise ValueError('Unsupported env script interpreter: ' + label)
+                add('usr/bin/' + fields[1])
+        if not python_added and re.fullmatch(r'usr/bin/python3(?:\.[0-9]+)?', label):
+            python_added = True
+            libraries = sorted((source.root / 'usr/lib').glob('python3.*'))
+            if not libraries:
+                raise ValueError('Missing Python standard library')
+            for library in libraries:
+                if library.is_dir():
+                    tree_files(library.relative_to(source.root).as_posix())
+        needed, paths, interpreter = dependencies(source.root / label)
+        if interpreter:
+            add(interpreter)
+        origin = str(PurePosixPath(label).parent)
+        if any(not p.startswith(('/', '$ORIGIN', '${ORIGIN}')) for p in paths):
+            raise ValueError('Relative ELF search path depends on runtime directory')
+        paths = [p.replace('${ORIGIN}', origin).replace('$ORIGIN', origin).lstrip('/') for p in paths]
+        if any('$' in p for p in paths):
+            raise ValueError('Unsupported ELF search variable')
+        for name in needed:
+            candidates = [normalized(p + '/' + name) for p in [*paths, 'usr/lib', 'lib']]
+            found = next((p for p in candidates if (source.root / source.resolve(p)).is_file()), None)
+            if found is None:
+                raise ValueError(f'Unresolved ELF dependency: {label} needs {name}')
+            add(found)
+    return selected, total
+
+
+def stage(source, selected, target):
+    target = Path(target)
+    if target.exists():
+        raise ValueError('Choose a new subset staging directory')
+    target.mkdir()
+    directories = {''}
+    for label, link in source.links.items():
+        if not (source.root / label).is_symlink() or os.readlink(source.root / label) != link:
+            raise ValueError('Source symlink changed during staging: ' + label)
+    for label in selected:
+        src, dst = source.root / label, target / label
+        if source.resolve(label) != label:
+            raise ValueError('Source path changed during staging: ' + label)
+        info = src.stat()
+        expected = selected[label]
+        if (digest(src) != expected['sha256'] or info.st_size != expected['bytes'] or
+                (stat.S_IMODE(info.st_mode), info.st_uid, info.st_gid) !=
+                (expected['mode'], expected['uid'], expected['gid'])):
+            raise ValueError('Source changed during staging: ' + label)
+        dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+        shutil.copy2(src, dst)
+        if digest(dst) != selected[label]['sha256']:
+            raise ValueError('Subset copy differs: ' + label)
+        info = src.stat()
+        if (info.st_uid, info.st_gid) != (dst.stat().st_uid, dst.stat().st_gid):
+            os.chown(dst, info.st_uid, info.st_gid)
+        directories.update(str(p) for p in PurePosixPath(label).parents if str(p) != '.')
+    for label in sorted(directories, key=lambda n: n.count('/'), reverse=True):
+        src, dst = source.root / label, target / label
+        info = src.stat()
+        dst.chmod(stat.S_IMODE(info.st_mode))
+        if (info.st_uid, info.st_gid) != (dst.stat().st_uid, dst.stat().st_gid):
+            os.chown(dst, info.st_uid, info.st_gid)
+    for label, link in sorted(source.links.items(), key=lambda pair: pair[0].count('/')):
+        dst = target / label
+        if dst.exists() or dst.is_symlink():
+            raise ValueError('Symlink collides with selected files: ' + label)
+        dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+        dst.symlink_to(link)
+
+
+def verify_inputs(root, desktop, receipt, packages):
+    metadata = json.loads(Path(desktop, 'manifest.json').read_text())
+    manifest = Path(desktop, 'payload/arch-ipad-ui-manifest.json')
+    if digest(manifest) != metadata['payload_manifest_sha256']:
+        raise ValueError('Normal desktop component manifest differs')
+    if digest(Path(root, 'arch-ipad-ui-manifest.json')) != metadata['payload_manifest_sha256']:
+        raise ValueError('Staged root does not contain this desktop component')
+    base = json.loads(Path(receipt).read_text())
+    if digest(packages) != base['packages_lock_sha256']:
+        raise ValueError('Normal root packages.lock differs')
+    return {'base_receipt': base, 'desktop_manifest_sha256': digest(Path(desktop, 'manifest.json')),
+            'packages_lock_sha256': digest(packages)}
+
+
+def verify_component_selection(source, selected, desktop):
+    payload = Path(desktop, 'payload')
+    contents = json.loads((payload / 'arch-ipad-ui-manifest.json').read_text())
+    for label, metadata in selected.items():
+        if label in contents and metadata['sha256'] != contents[label]:
+            raise ValueError('Selected desktop file differs from normal component: ' + label)
+    for label, link in source.links.items():
+        original = payload / label
+        if label in contents or (original.is_symlink() and os.readlink(original) != link):
+            raise ValueError('Selected desktop symlink differs from normal component: ' + label)
+
+
+def produce(root, desktop, receipt, packages, output, *, compressed_limit=128 * 1024**2,
+            expanded_limit=384 * 1024**2, upper_mib=64, plan_only=False):
+    output = Path(output)
+    if output.exists() or output.is_symlink() or not 16 <= upper_mib <= 128:
+        raise ValueError('Choose a new output and an upper limit of 16..128 MiB')
+    provenance = verify_inputs(root, desktop, receipt, packages)
+    source = Source(root)
+    selected, total = selection(source, [*FILES, *('usr/bin/' + p for p in PROGRAMS)], TREES,
+                                 expanded_limit=expanded_limit)
+    verify_component_selection(source, selected, desktop)
+    record = {'schema': 1, 'kind': 'ram-desktop-candidate', 'status': 'HOST_PLAN_ONLY',
+              'source': provenance, 'selected': selected, 'symlinks': source.links,
+              'expanded_bytes': total, 'expanded_limit': expanded_limit,
+              'compressed_limit': compressed_limit, 'upper_mib': upper_mib,
+              'device_tested': False, 'full_installed_omarchy': False,
+              'source_archive_rechecked': False}
+    output.mkdir(parents=True)
+    if not plan_only:
+        subset = output / '.subset'
+        stage(source, selected, subset)
+        project = output / 'project'
+        image = project / 'rootfs/usr/share/omarchy/desktop.squashfs'
+        image.parent.mkdir(parents=True)
+        subprocess.run(['mksquashfs', str(subset), str(image), '-noappend', '-comp', 'gzip',
+                        '-b', '262144', '-processors', '1', '-mem', '128M', '-no-xattrs',
+                        '-no-exports', '-mkfs-time', '0', '-all-time', '0'], check=True)
+        if image.stat().st_size > compressed_limit:
+            raise ValueError('Compressed desktop exceeds the declared RAM limit')
+        shutil.copyfile(PROJECT / 'system/ram-desktop/init', project / 'init')
+        (project / 'init').chmod(0o755)
+        session = project / 'rootfs/usr/libexec/omarchy/ram-desktop'
+        session.parent.mkdir(parents=True)
+        shutil.copyfile(PROJECT / 'system/ram-desktop/session', session)
+        session.chmod(0o755)
+        (project / 'rootfs/etc').mkdir(parents=True)
+        (project / 'rootfs/etc/omarchy-ram-upper-mib').write_text(str(upper_mib) + '\n')
+        (project / 'orchard.toml').write_text('name = "omarchy-ram-desktop"\n\n[payload]\ntransport = true\nmodules = true\nfirmware = true\n')
+        record.update(status='HOST_BUILT_DEVICE_UNTESTED', compressed_bytes=image.stat().st_size,
+                      image_sha256=digest(image), project='project')
+        shutil.rmtree(subset)
+    (output / 'ram-desktop.json').write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + '\n')
+    return record
diff --git a/system/ram-desktop/init b/system/ram-desktop/init
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..60bc627
--- /dev/null
+++ b/system/ram-desktop/init
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+#!/bin/busybox sh
+# Experimental RAM desktop. Hardware comes from Orchard's matching kernel.
+set -eu
+export PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
+/bin/busybox --install -s /bin
+mount -t proc -o nosuid,nodev,noexec proc /proc
+mount -t sysfs -o nosuid,nodev,noexec sysfs /sys
+mount -t devtmpfs -o nosuid devtmpfs /dev
+mount -t tmpfs -o nosuid,nodev tmpfs /run
+mkdir -p /dev/pts /tmp
+mount -t devpts -o nosuid devpts /dev/pts
+exec </dev/console >/dev/console 2>&1
+echo /bin/false > /proc/sys/kernel/modprobe
+echo /bin/false > /proc/sys/kernel/hotplug
+
+# Keep the ordinary host key, serial console and SSH outside the desktop root.
+sh /usr/libexec/orchard/usb-session || echo 'USB session startup failed'
+(
+    while :; do
+        setsid -c sh -i </dev/ttyGS0 >/dev/ttyGS0 2>&1 || true
+        sleep 1
+    done
+) &
+echo 'RAM console ready; no desktop, optional drivers or internal storage activated.'
+echo 'After hardware checks, use normal orchard exec to run:'
+echo '  /usr/libexec/omarchy/ram-desktop start'
+while :; do sleep 60; done
diff --git a/system/ram-desktop/session b/system/ram-desktop/session
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..45fd9d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/system/ram-desktop/session
@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+#!/bin/busybox sh
+# A manually started chroot session; PID 1 and the standard SSH keys stay outside.
+set -eu
+export PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
+pidfile=/run/omarchy-ram.pid
+state=/run/omarchy-ram-state
+lock=/run/omarchy-ram-owner
+case "${1:-}" in
+start)
+    [ ! -e "$pidfile" ] || { echo 'Session ownership exists; inspect status first'; exit 1; }
+    mkdir "$lock" || { echo 'Session start/cleanup ownership exists'; exit 1; }
+    setsid sh "$0" run </dev/null >/run/omarchy-ram-session.log 2>&1 &
+    pid=$!
+    [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ]
+    printf '%s %s\n' "$pid" "$(awk '{print $22}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" > "$pidfile"
+    echo START_REQUESTED
+    exit 0
+    ;;
+stop|status)
+    [ -r "$pidfile" ] || {
+        [ ! -e "$lock" ] || { echo 'Session ownership is incomplete; inspect logs'; exit 1; }
+        echo STOPPED; exit 0;
+    }
+    read -r pid born < "$pidfile"
+    case "$pid:$born" in *[!0-9:]*|:*|*:) echo 'Invalid session ownership'; exit 1;; esac
+    if [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ]; then
+        [ "$(awk '{print $22}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" = "$born" ] || { echo 'Session PID changed'; exit 1; }
+        if [ "$1" = stop ]; then
+            /bin/busybox kill -TERM -- "-$pid"
+            i=0
+            while [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ] && [ "$i" -lt 100 ]; do sleep .1; i=$((i + 1)); done
+            [ ! -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ] || { echo 'Session cleanup still pending'; exit 1; }
+            [ "$(cat "$state")" = STOPPED ] || { cat "$state"; exit 1; }
+        else
+            cat "$state" 2>/dev/null || echo STARTING
+        fi
+    else
+        cat "$state" 2>/dev/null || echo STOPPED
+        [ "$(cat "$state" 2>/dev/null)" != CLEANUP_FAILED ] || exit 1
+    fi
+    exit 0
+    ;;
+run)
+    # Internal child only: refuse direct/concurrent runtime entry points.
+    i=0
+    while [ ! -r "$pidfile" ] && [ "$i" -lt 20 ]; do sleep .1; i=$((i + 1)); done
+    [ -d "$lock" ] && [ -r "$pidfile" ] || exit 1
+    read -r owner born < "$pidfile"
+    [ "$owner" = "$$" ] && [ "$(awk '{print $22}' "/proc/$$/stat")" = "$born" ] || exit 1
+    ;;
+*) echo 'Usage: ram-desktop start|stop|status'; exit 2;;
+esac
+
+lower=/run/omarchy-lower
+writable=/run/omarchy-writable
+desktop=/run/omarchy-desktop
+children=/run/omarchy-ram-children
+: > "$children"
+echo STARTING > "$state"
+cleanup() {
+    failed=0
+    while read -r pid born; do
+        [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ] || continue
+        [ "$(awk '{print $22}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" = "$born" ] || { failed=1; continue; }
+        /bin/busybox kill -TERM -- "-$pid" 2>/dev/null || true
+    done < "$children"
+    # Bounded normal exit; keep mounts and ownership on a stuck process.
+    i=0
+    while [ "$i" -lt 50 ]; do
+        alive=0
+        while read -r pid born; do
+            if [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ]; then
+                case "$(awk '{print $3}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" in Z) wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true;; *) alive=1;; esac
+            fi
+        done < "$children"
+        [ "$alive" = 0 ] && break
+        sleep .1; i=$((i + 1))
+    done
+    if [ "$alive" != 0 ] || [ "$failed" != 0 ]; then echo CLEANUP_FAILED > "$state"; return; fi
+    for name in run sys proc dev/shm dev/pts dev; do
+        if mountpoint -q "$desktop/$name"; then umount "$desktop/$name" || failed=1; fi
+    done
+    for path in "$desktop" "$writable" "$lower"; do
+        if mountpoint -q "$path"; then umount "$path" || failed=1; fi
+    done
+    if [ "$failed" = 0 ]; then echo STOPPED > "$state"; rm -f "$pidfile"; rmdir "$lock";
+    else echo CLEANUP_FAILED > "$state"; fi
+}
+trap 'exit 0' TERM INT
+trap cleanup EXIT
+mkdir -p "$lower" "$writable" "$desktop"
+upper_mib=$(cat /etc/omarchy-ram-upper-mib)
+case "$upper_mib" in ''|*[!0-9]*) exit 1;; esac
+[ "$upper_mib" -ge 16 ] && [ "$upper_mib" -le 128 ]
+mount -t squashfs -o loop,ro /usr/share/omarchy/desktop.squashfs "$lower"
+mount -t tmpfs -o "size=${upper_mib}m,nr_inodes=32768,mode=0755" tmpfs "$writable"
+mkdir "$writable/upper" "$writable/work"
+mount -t overlay overlay -o "lowerdir=$lower,upperdir=$writable/upper,workdir=$writable/work" "$desktop"
+mkdir -p "$desktop/dev/pts" "$desktop/proc" "$desktop/sys" "$desktop/run"
+for name in dev dev/pts proc sys; do mount --bind "/$name" "$desktop/$name"; done
+mkdir -p "$desktop/dev/shm"
+mount -t tmpfs -o size=16m,nr_inodes=4096,mode=1777,nosuid,nodev tmpfs "$desktop/dev/shm"
+# A private bounded /run avoids recursively binding the parent /run into itself.
+mount -t tmpfs -o size=32m,nr_inodes=8192,mode=0755 tmpfs "$desktop/run"
+mkdir -p "$desktop/tmp" "$desktop/run/user/1000" "$desktop/run/dbus" "$desktop/run/udev"
+chmod 1777 "$desktop/tmp"
+chmod 700 "$desktop/run/user/1000"
+chown 1000:1000 "$desktop/run/user/1000"
+# A new per-boot machine ID lives only in the RAM upper. The staged root has
+# no installed machine identity, and no host/system machine ID is copied.
+chroot "$desktop" /usr/bin/dbus-uuidgen --ensure=/etc/machine-id
+if [ -f /etc/resolv.conf ]; then cat /etc/resolv.conf > "$desktop/etc/resolv.conf"; fi
+spawn() {
+    setsid chroot "$desktop" "$@" &
+    pid=$!
+    [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ]
+    printf '%s %s\n' "$pid" "$(awk '{print $22}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" >> "$children"
+}
+spawn /usr/lib/systemd/systemd-udevd --resolve-names=never
+spawn /usr/bin/dbus-daemon --system --nofork
+spawn /usr/bin/seatd -g seat
+sleep 1
+# Only describe already-created input/DRM nodes to libinput. No bus coldplug.
+chroot "$desktop" /usr/bin/udevadm trigger --action=add --subsystem-match=input
+chroot "$desktop" /usr/bin/udevadm trigger --action=add --subsystem-match=drm
+chroot "$desktop" /usr/bin/udevadm settle --timeout=10
+spawn /usr/bin/setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups /usr/bin/env \
+    HOME=/home/tablet USER=tablet LOGNAME=tablet PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin \
+    LANG=C.UTF-8 LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000 \
+    XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=wlroots LIBSEAT_BACKEND=seatd \
+    WLR_BACKENDS=drm,libinput WLR_RENDERER=pixman QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software \
+    QSG_RENDER_LOOP=basic QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland OMARCHY_TOUCH_MODE=1 \
+    OMARCHY_KEYBOARD_AUTO=1 OMARCHY_PATH=/home/tablet/.local/share/omarchy-ipad \
+    /usr/bin/dbus-run-session /bin/bash -ec \
+    '/usr/local/libexec/arch-ipad-first-theme; exec /usr/bin/labwc -m'
+echo PROCESSES_STARTED_UI_UNVERIFIED > "$state"
+while :; do
+    while read -r pid born; do
+        [ -r "/proc/$pid/stat" ] || exit 1
+        [ "$(awk '{print $22}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" = "$born" ] || exit 1
+        [ "$(awk '{print $3}' "/proc/$pid/stat")" != Z ] || exit 1
+    done < "$children"
+    sleep 1
+done
